<title>UK: BAA Plc up after upbeat presentation.</title>
<headline>BAA Plc up after upbeat presentation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BAA Plc crept higher as the broad market slipped after the airport facility manager delivered an upbeat presentation at London's Heathrow airport on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0817 GMT, the shares were up 7p to 502p.  </p>
<p>Also supporting BAA shares were weekend press reports that the Office of Fair Trading will recommend that the government clears the planned merger between British Airways and AMR's American Airlines on conditions that will be accepted by both carriers, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;Anything that will lead to increased traffic is going to help BAA,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
